{"body":"## Problem\n\nIn Docker isolation, a command that starts with a shell and `-c` but is **more than** `sh -c '<script>'` is rewritten before it runs, and the rewrite changes what it does. Reproduced on 0.35.4 with the code unchanged on `main` (2f4273d); attached and detached both affected:\n\n```sh\n$ -i docker -a --image <img> --shell sh -- \"sh -c 'exit 7'; echo OUT after \\$?\"\n$ sh -c \"exit 7; echo OUT after $?\"        # <- shown and executed\nExit Code:  7                              # expected: prints \"OUT after 7\", exits 0\n\n$ -i docker -a --image <img> --shell sh -- \"sh -c 'sleep 1; kill -9 \\$\\$'; exit \\$?\"\n$ sh -c \"sleep 1; kill -9 $$; exit $?\"     # trailing `; exit $?` pulled into the -c script\n# exits 0, while plain `docker run <img> sh -c \"<same command>\"` exits 137\n```\n\nThe same command without isolation (`$ -- \"sh -c 'exit 7'; echo OUT after \\$?\"`) prints `OUT after 7`, so there only the displayed form is wrong.\n\nWe hit this while testing an auto-fix tool. A deliberate `kill -9` test task finished with **exit 0** in the record and in Docker. A real killed task with a command of that shape would be recorded as a success: a false negative for every OOM or kill detection built on start-command.\n\n## Cause\n\n`js/src/lib/shell-utils.js`:\n\n- `isShellInvocationWithArgs(command)` is true whenever the first word is a shell name and `-c` appears **anywhere** among the words.\n- `buildShellWithArgsCmdArgs(command)` then takes `parts.slice(cIdx + 1).join(' ')` as the script. That folds in:\n  - everything after the script: `; echo …`, `&& …`, `| …`;\n  - the positional arguments: `sh -c 'echo $1' x y` becomes the script `echo $1 x y`, so `$0`/`$1` are lost;\n  - all quoting.\n- `isolation.js` (~617 detached, ~737 attached) executes those argv for Docker; `buildDisplayCommand` shows the same rewritten form everywhere.\n\n## Fix\n\nTreat a command as a direct shell invocation only when its words are exactly `<shell> [shell flags] -c <script> [arg0 [args...]]`, with no unquoted shell operators (`;`, `&&`, `||`, `|`, `&`, redirections) outside the script word. Pass `<script>` as one argv element and the rest as separate argv elements, never joined into the script. Anything else is a shell command line: run it with `<shell> -c <whole command line>`, as the non-isolated path already does.\n\nTests:\n- `sh -c 'exit 7'; echo after $?` → prints `after 7`, exits 0\n- `sh -c 'echo $0 $1' a b` → prints `a b`\n- `sh -c 'sleep 1; kill -9 $$'; exit $?` → exit 137\n- `bash -i -c \"nvm --version\"` (#91) still runs directly\n\nRelated: #91, #164.\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\n\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-10T11:25:19Z","title":"Docker isolation rewrites 'sh -c <script>; more' into 'sh -c \"<script>; more\"': trailing commands, $0/$1 args and quoting folded into the -c script (exit codes lost, kill -9 recorded as exit 0)","updatedAt":"2026-10-10T11:25:19Z","url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/start/issues/202"}
